WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.130
Take a sheet of paper, about
nought point one millimetres thick,

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.850
and fold it in half.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.830
One layer becomes two.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.860
Fold again: four.

5
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.080
Then eight.

6
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.970
Then sixteen.

7
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.120
This is a thought experiment.

8
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:18.890
Real paper can't be folded
anywhere near forty-two times.

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.770
But if you could, would
the stack reach the Moon,

10
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.990
about three hundred and
eighty-four thousand,

11
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.170
four hundred kilometres away?

12
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.310
In this mission, you'll write
repeated doubling as a power of two.

13
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.380
You'll learn the laws of indices.

14
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.840
And a shortcut: two to the
ten is about a thousand,

15
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.280
so two to the forty is
about ten to the twelve.

16
00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: work out whether
forty-two folds would reach the Moon.
